# EditMode tests — when to run what

## With the Editor open (normal workflow)

- **Window → General → Test Runner** → **Edit Mode** tab → select assembly **Forbes.Tests.EditMode** → **Run All** (or run a single fixture).
- This works while the project is open; you do **not** need batchmode or to close Unity.

## From the shell (CI, or when you can close the Editor)

- Batch Unity **cannot** open the same project twice. `tools\Run-EditModeTests.ps1` requires the **Editor closed** for this project.

  ```text
  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools\Run-EditModeTests.ps1
  ```

- Results: `TestResults-EditMode.xml`.

# CLI verification

- When the user reports **compile errors**, **broken tests**, or **Console errors tied to gameplay/C#**, prefer **Test Runner (Edit Mode)** in the open Editor. Use batchmode when feasible:

  ```text
  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools\Run-EditModeTests.ps1
  ```

  from repo root (**Unity batchmode rejects a locked project** — close the Editor on this project first, or run tests inside the Editor as above).

- Read `TestResults-EditMode.xml` for failures when using batchmode; fix code and re-run.

- Do not declare "fixed" without a green test run when the failure was in compilable/gameplay C#.
